# A Game: Full Title

PARAMETERS: everything in this file is the project's own. Keep the seven headings below, in this order; the scaffold check compares them by text. Copy to README.md.

A matching decompilation of **A Game: Full Title** (GameCube, 2002). The goal is source that compiles back to a byte-identical copy of each original executable, with names, types and source structure supported by evidence.

## Targets

| Id | Region | Revision | Status | Original SHA-1 |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `GAME01-rev0` | USA | 0 | active | `0000000000000000000000000000000000000000` |
| `GAME01-rev1` | USA | 1 | planned | `1111111111111111111111111111111111111111` |

`config/targets.json` is the registry; each target's inputs are in `config/<id>/`.

## Building

You need your own copy of each game disc. Keep disc images and extracted files outside public Git.

1. Place the original at `orig/<id>/sys/main.dol`.
2. `python3 configure.py --version <id>` then `ninja -f build/<id>/build.ninja`. The build fails unless the relinked executable matches `config/<id>/build.sha1`.
3. `ninja -f build/<id>/build.ninja progress build/<id>/report.json` measures the target.

To check every active target: `for id in $(python3 -c 'from tools.targets import build_targets; print(*build_targets())'); do python3 configure.py --version "$id" && ninja -f "build/$id/build.ninja"; done`.

Pinned tool versions are in `configure.py`; the build structure is [dtk-template](https://github.com/encounter/dtk-template) at the revision named in `CREDITS.md`.

## CI and the progress site

`.github/workflows/validate.yml` builds every affected target in the private build image and publishes each measurement to the [progress site](https://mitsevox.github.io/games/game/) on `main`. Pull requests publish nothing.

